---
/**
 * Cursor — the custom cursor follower (`a-8` Cursor Move, `a-165`/`a-166` Cursor View
 * Show/Hide). Phase E.
 *
 * ⚠️ This markup did not exist in the rebuild. Phases B and C skipped it because it is
 * presentational scaffolding with no content and `components.md` #8 filed it as optional.
 * The structure below is the source's verbatim, from `_webflow-export/index.html`:
 *
 *   <div class="cursor-wrapper"><div class="cursor"><div class="cursor-text view">View</div></div></div>
 *
 * ── Scope: five pages, and NOT via BaseLayout ─────────────────────────────────────────
 * interactions.md's Phase E readiness map verified this markup against every exported page
 * and every captured live page. It is present on `/`, `/services`, `/team`, `/projects` and
 * `/contact` — and absent from all five `/project/<slug>` pages, all three legal pages, and
 * `/404` (those carry the `.cursor-wrapper { pointer-events: none }` rule in their inline
 * `<style>` but no element to apply it to). Putting this in `BaseLayout` would add it to
 * nine pages that never had it, which is a design change rather than a migration — so it is
 * imported per page instead.
 *
 * `.cursor` starts `display: none`, so on `/services`, `/team` and `/contact` — which have
 * no `.project-card-image-wrapper` to hover — the element is inert and never paints. That
 * matches the source, where those pages ship the markup but nothing ever shows it.
 *
 * Styles are the source's `.cursor-wrapper` / `.cursor` rules verbatim, expressed through
 * the existing tokens. There is no `.cursor-text` or `.view` rule in the source CSS — those
 * divs inherit everything from `.cursor`; their only role is being toggled by `a-165`.
 * `transform` is deliberately absent from the CSS: `cursor.ts` is the single writer of that
 * property, because the rAF translate and the scale tween would otherwise clobber each other.
 */
---

<div class="cursor-wrapper" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="cursor">
    <div class="cursor-text view">View</div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .cursor-wrapper {
    z-index: var(--z-overlay);
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    /* Source: the follower is drawn *alongside* the native cursor — the source CSS has no
       `cursor: none` anywhere — so it must never intercept a click. */
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 0.3s;
  }

  .cursor {
    display: none;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    /* Hotspot offset — verbatim from source. */
    margin-top: -1rem;
    margin-left: -1rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    background-color: var(--color-ink);
    color: var(--color-on-ink);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono-md);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 120%;
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
    text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* Suppression, not shortening — interactions.md §3 lists a-8/a-165/a-166 as "suppress
     entirely". `cursor.ts` additionally refuses to mount its rAF loop under this preference
     and re-evaluates on change; this rule is the belt to that braces, and it lives here
     rather than in global.css so that a scoped `display: flex` can never out-order it. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cursor-wrapper {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import '../scripts/cursor'
</script>
